---@class UcPlayerHandle
---@field present boolean True while the player exists in the current scene. [implemented]
---@field magazine integer Rounds left in the loaded magazine of the current weapon. [implemented]
---@field grenades integer Grenades in stock. [implemented]
---@field damage number The damage meter: 0 is unhurt, 50 is dead. Writing 0 heals. [implemented]
---@field invulnerable boolean While true the damage meter is reset to 0 every game step. [implemented]
---@field infinite_ammo boolean While true the magazine is refilled to its starting size every game step. [implemented]
---@field weapon integer The weapon id the player holds (0 to 19: the record number of the weapon table, 0 and 19 are the handgun). Read only: switching weapons runs game logic a plain write would skip. [implemented]
---@field health number Health as a fraction: 1 unhurt, 0 dead. The damage meter turned around (health = 1 - damage / 50), so setting it writes the meter. [implemented]
---@field reserve integer The spare ammo of the weapon the player holds (0 to 9999), per player. nil / null for the handgun, whose reserve is infinite (setting it is an error). Confirmed: a reload takes the rounds it loads off this count. [implemented]

---@class UcWeaponHandle
---@field damage number Damage per hit (per pellet for a shotgun): the handgun's 10 takes a zombie down in two hits. Checked in the game: with 100 a hit takes 100 off a zombie (the body, head and limb multipliers stay). [implemented]
---@field fire_rate number Shots per second, 0.05 to 60 (the handgun is 1; submachine guns 10 to 15). The game turns the rate into an interval (1 / rate) when a weapon is equipped; the API sets both the record and the interval of players holding the weapon, and keeps them. Checked in the game with automatic fire: a rate of 2 gives about twice the shots in the same time, 0.25 four times as many as 1. Semi-automatic weapons need `fire_mode = 'auto'` for the rate to matter while the trigger is held. [implemented]
---@field capacity integer Magazine size, 0 to 999. The game reads it when a reload ends: with 30 set for the handgun a reload refills 30 rounds. [implemented]
---@field reload_time number Reload duration in seconds of game time (1.0 for the handgun, 2.3 for a shotgun); 0.2 makes a handgun reload about seven times faster. [implemented]
---@field fire_mode string 'semi' (one shot per press), 'auto' (shots repeat while the button is held) or 'burst'. 'auto' on the handgun was checked in the game (a held trigger fires about every 22 frames instead of once); 'burst' is the value the game's record 3 uses and its effect on other weapons is untested. Reading a value the table holds that has no name gives 'mode <number>'. [implemented]

