---Callbacks on selected game functions. Only the functions listed under 'Hookable functions' accept hooks (the list grows with releases); each hook point costs nothing while no mod uses it.
hook = {}

---Names of the hookable functions. [implemented]
---@return string[]
function hook.list() end

---Runs a callback before the game function. The callback may change the registers it is given (they are written back). [implemented]
---@param name string A hookable function name.
---@param callback function Called before the function runs with a table of its registers: r3..r10 as integers, f1..f8 as floats.
function hook.pre(name, callback) end

---Runs a callback after the game function returned, also after a replacement. Needs touches_gameplay. [implemented]
---@param name string A hookable function name.
---@param callback function Called after the function returned with a table of its registers: r3 and f1 hold the return value and may be changed.
function hook.post(name, callback) end

---Replaces the game function: the original body does not run (pre hooks still run before, post hooks after). Several replacements all run, in install order. Needs touches_gameplay. [implemented]
---@param name string A hookable function name.
---@param callback function Runs instead of the function, with a table of its argument registers; set r3 and f1 to the return value.
function hook.replace(name, callback) end

